omar: Heads-up: intermittent "Unexpected end of JSON input" in the Node SDK when consuming SSE. Seen in onboarding sample with node 18 + sdk-js. Seems to spike when users close the tab mid-stream or when runtime rotates auth. Anyone else?

vikas: yep, saw a similar report. Node code assumes 'data:' events arrive whole. Proxies/TCP can split a single event across chunks so JSON.parse can get half a payload.

tori: runtime note: when we rotate auth we sometimes close and re-open the SSE connection without any resume metadata. That can cause loss of in-flight bytes.

maya: python patched this by keeping a persistent tail and only parsing on the SSE delimiter, but node doesn't currently. Also server-provided seq numbers make detection easier.

omar: repro snippet (naive):```js
res.on('data', chunk => {
  const s = chunk.toString();
  const evs = s.split('\n\n');
  evs.forEach(e => {
    if (e.startsWith('data: ')) {
      const o = JSON.parse(e.slice(6)); // blows up if split mid-json
      onEvent(o);
    }
  });
});```

vikas: small fix: maintain a tail buffer across data events and across reconnects. Example:```js
let tail = '';
res.on('data', c => {
  tail += c.toString();
  let idx;
  while ((idx = tail.indexOf('\n\n')) !== -1) {
    const raw = tail.slice(0, idx);
    tail = tail.slice(idx + 2);
    if (raw.startsWith('data: ')) {
      try { handle(JSON.parse(raw.slice(6))); } catch (err) { /* stash and retry after reconnect */ }
    }
  }
});
// preserve `tail` when reconnecting and prepend to next stream
```

tori: runtime-side action: for planned rotates we can emit `event: control` pre-rotate with a last_seq. For forced rotates we'll try to include resume info on the new stream. Will open a PR to standardize the control event shape.

maya: recommend SDKs optionally validate seq continuity when `seq` is provided in payloads and surface telemetry like `sse_resume_gap` if discontinuities are detected.

ovik: (typo fixed) vikas: I'll file a node SDK issue and add unit tests simulating split chunks, aborts, and auth rotate. Also add telemetry `sse_parse_error`.

ci-bot: Created issue #4721: "sdk-js(node): SSE partial-chunk parse errors on reconnect/auth-rotate - add tail buffer & seq handling" assigned to vikas.
